the obama era daca program will reach  its 10th anniversary this year as part  of that milestone dozens of scholarships  are up for grabs to help the so-called  dreamers further their education  christian casares joining us live in our  studio with more on who christian is  behind the effort well brian daca which  is short for the deferred action for  childhood arrivals program has helped  thousands thousands of undocumented  immigrants over the past 10 years and  now the mexican consulate in las vegas  wants to help for one local dreamer that  helping hand could mean a college degree  every little bit of money is incredibly  helpful you know like either it pays for  my school or pays for my transportation  22 year old daniel lara works hard every  day to achieve his dream of becoming a  college graduate a dream that he says is  difficult to obtain because of his legal  status i needed a job that was legal and  i needed to be able to apply to you know  higher education and i couldn't be able  to do that without any sort of  you know legality in the country laura  is one of the estimated 11 000  beneficiaries in nevada enrolled in the  daca program according to the mexican  consulate in las vegas the obama air  initiative provides legal status and  work permits for undocumented immigrants  brought to the country as children as it  reaches its first decade more help is on  the way many undocumented youth do not  have access to financial financial  assistance so we do have  a scholarship program that is open now  for applications up to 2500 will be  awarded to an estimated 50 daca winners  to further their education thanks to  private donations funds that the council  of mexico and las vegas says can go a  long way for those with limited to no  resources they do not have access to  financial assistance there's no federal  or state  programs for them since 2017 laura has  taken full advantage of the benefits of  the daca program although daca has no  path to citizenship he says his  education is priceless if one day they  decide to take it out then it's like i  can't work go to work no more i can't go  to school no more  all right applications for the  scholarship are now open and the winners  will be announced on august 10th now if  you're interested we have a link to  apply on our website eight newsnow dot  com christian cousin is live local now
 

